        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "I identified the relevant work order as **WO-2025-09-004 / MO-25-09-1070** for the Racine operation. Its September cost period, **Sep-25**, was recorded as **PENDING_CLOSE** at **2025-09-30T18:00:00**.\n\nI could not verify whether an event was created after that time or report its source transaction ID, amount, created time, lateness, or accounting status. Those event-level details are not in the resource available to my assigned-analyst role; the supporting records and their mirror are restricted to the records-custodian role. I did not access those restricted records or change any database records.\n\nThe accessible Oracle 26B policy excerpt says new transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged for Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting until the period is closed or reopened; transactions created after the Pending Close date are not processed. **Without the event row, I cannot determine whether its recorded status is consistent with that treatment.**\n\nI submitted the report as incomplete for lack of evidence and notified the supervisor that authorized custodian access is needed to finish the review.",
